      <section>
        <h2>How to Pay</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cash (USD):</strong> Most common at entry gates. Bring clean, undamaged post-2013 series bills.</li>
          <li><strong>Card:</strong> Available at Mnemba, Menai Bay, Jozani main gates (Visa/Mastercard).</li>
          <li><strong>Mobile Money:</strong> M-Pesa, Tigo Pesa, Airtel Money (TZS equivalent).</li>
          <li><strong>Pre-paid via Tour Operator:</strong> Most Spice & Sail tours <strong>include all conservation fees</strong> — no extra payment on the day.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="card" style="padding:1.5rem;background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #4caf50;margin:1.5rem 0;">
          <h3 style="margin-top:0;">✅ Spice & Sail Tours Include Fees</h3>
          <p style="margin:0;">When you book Mnemba Snorkeling, Safari Blue, Jozani Forest, or Prison Island with us, <strong>all marine park/conservation fees are included</strong> in your quoted price. No surprise payments on the boat or at the gate.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Fee Exemptions & Reductions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>EAC Residents:</strong> Kenya, Uganda, Rwanda, Burundi, South Sudan, DRC, Tanzania — show valid residency permit.</li>
          <li><strong>Tanzanian Citizens:</strong> Show National ID or passport — pay in TZS at citizen rate.</li>
          <li><strong>Children under 5:</strong> Free at most sites.</li>
          <li><strong>Children 5–15:</strong> 50% discount at most marine parks.</li>
          <li><strong>Students/Researchers:</strong> With valid institutional letter — apply in advance to park authority.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <details><summary>Do I pay the fee every time I enter?</summary><p>Yes, most marine park fees are <strong>per entry, per person</strong>. If you do Mnemba snorkeling on two separate days, you pay twice. Some multi-day liveaboards include multiple entries.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I pay in Tanzanian Shillings?</summary><p>At major gates (Mnemba, Menai Bay, Jozani) yes — at the official daily rate. At smaller sites (turtle ponds, caves), often USD only. Carry small USD bills.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What if I don't have cash?</summary><p>Major gates accept Visa/Mastercard. If card machines are down (happens), you may need to return with cash. We recommend carrying $50–100 in small USD bills for fees, tips, and markets.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Are fees the same for snorkeling vs diving?</summary><p>Yes, the conservation fee is the same regardless of activity. Dive operators may charge additional boat/gear fees on top.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Where does the money go?</summary><p>Published annual reports from Mnemba, Menai Bay, Chumbe, and Jozani show allocation: ~40% ranger operations, ~25% community projects, ~20% conservation programs, ~15% administration.</p></details>
      </section>

